`CVConfig.score_by` names a `sample_metadata` column to also score by. Every metric then gets a second fold score, `<metric>_by_<column>`, computed after averaging the test predictions that share a value: for example one prediction per recording, from the same fit that gives the per-epoch scores, while the folds stay grouped by subject. It replaces `CVConfig.score_by_group`, which pooled by the fold groups only and reported the pooled scores instead of the per-sample ones.
